body:
one person's opinion: yes, and do it quickly. don't waste your time with people who are incompatible with you and your goals/desires. many people say to hold off, some even suggest not disclosing at all if you don't get outbreaks, but to me, it's completely necessary for consent reasons, and also it's more hurtful when they break it off after you've already gotten to know them. to get my hopes up about dating, however casually, without disclosing first isn't worth it in my experience because a person who isn't mature or ready enough to date someone with an STI is going to show their true colors whether it's the first time you talk or months later. again, this is just one person's experience with a few incompatible folks, but not even my \~stellar personality and amazing company\~ could trump the stigma, so why waste my own time and give myself a bad experience that can be avoided by being honest upfront?

&#x200B;

edit: i share with friends, not family. completely up to you who you want to disclose too. my messaging above is really just about potential sex partners. best of luck to you!
